IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division E: sections 40 and 41. LAYER 1, from the text alone.
--
-- Section 40 is the Governor in Council's power to make regulations for Part I. Most of it is machinery and is not encoded
-- (the coverage table in NOTES.md gives each paragraph a row and a reason). What it decides for a person is encoded here: the ceiling
-- on a penalty a regulation may set for not filing an information return (paragraph 40(1)(d)), the day the regulation prescribing
-- the deduction rules takes effect (subsection (3)), and when an agreement may reach back in time (subsection (4)).
-- Section 41 creates the offences of Part I: an employer who does not deduct and remit, a person who does not keep records, a
-- person who does not file a return, and a person who makes false statements, destroys records or evades. Each offence is a
-- constitutive BOOLEAN over the elements the section states; the most (and, where stated, the least) the court may impose is a
-- separate rule, a ceiling and not an amount (phrasebook 5.7). The sentence actually passed is a fact about a case.
-- "The most" is NOTHING where the section names no maximum, never a plausible figure.
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars and a term of imprisonment a NUMBER of months.

§ `Division E -- Regulations and Offences`

§§ `s 40 -- what the regulation-making power decides for a person`

-- (1)(d): "a penalty not exceeding ten dollars a day for each day of default and not exceeding in all two hundred and fifty dollars".
-- src:882 | (d) prescribing a penalty not exceeding ten dollars a day for each day of default and not exceeding in all two hundred and fifty dollars to which a person who fails to comply with a regulation made under paragraph (b) or (c) shall be liable;
@ref Act s 40(1)(d) (src:882)
GIVEN `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(1)(d) — the most a regulation may prescribe as the penalty for not filing an information return` `the number of days of default` MEANS
    min 250 (10 TIMES `the number of days of default`)

@ref Act s 40(1)(d) (src:882)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty a regulation prescribes` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(1)(d) — the penalty a regulation prescribes is within the limit the paragraph allows` `the amount of the penalty a regulation prescribes` `the number of days of default` MEANS
    `the amount of the penalty a regulation prescribes` AT MOST (`s 40(1)(d) — the most a regulation may prescribe as the penalty for not filing an information return` `the number of days of default`)

-- src:892 | Effective date of regulations
-- src:893 | (3) A regulation made under paragraph (1)(a) prescribing rules referred to in subsection 21(1) shall have effect from the day it is published in the Canada Gazette or from such earlier or later day as may be specified in the regulation.
@ref Act s 40(3) (src:892-893)
GIVEN `the day the regulation is published in the Canada Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulation specifies as the day it takes effect, if it specifies one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 40(3) — the day the regulation prescribing the rules for subsection 21(1) has effect from` `the day the regulation is published in the Canada Gazette` `the day the regulation specifies as the day it takes effect, if it specifies one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the regulation specifies as the day it takes effect, if it specifies one`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN specified
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the regulation is published in the Canada Gazette`

-- src:894 | Effective date of certain agreements
-- src:895 | (4) Any agreement for giving effect to the provisions of paragraph 6(2)(h) or 7(1)(f) that is entered into by the Minister pursuant to regulations made under paragraph (1)(h) has effect with reference to a period before it was entered into if the agreement provides for that effect.
@ref Act s 40(4) (src:894-895)
GIVEN `the agreement is for giving effect to the provisions of paragraph 6(2)(h) or 7(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister entered into the agreement pursuant to regulations made under paragraph 40(1)(h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides that it has effect with reference to a period before it was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) — the agreement has effect with reference to a period before it was entered into` `the agreement is for giving effect to the provisions of paragraph 6(2)(h) or 7(1)(f)` `the Minister entered into the agreement pursuant to regulations made under paragraph 40(1)(h)` `the agreement provides that it has effect with reference to a period before it was entered into` MEANS
        `the agreement is for giving effect to the provisions of paragraph 6(2)(h) or 7(1)(f)`
    AND `the Minister entered into the agreement pursuant to regulations made under paragraph 40(1)(h)`
    AND `the agreement provides that it has effect with reference to a period before it was entered into`

§§ `s 41(1) to (3) -- offences of the employer and of a person who does not keep records or file`

-- src:897 | Offences
-- src:898 | Offence and punishment
-- src:899 | 41 (1) Every employer who fails to comply with subsection 21(1) or 23(3) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to
-- src:900 | (a) a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars; or
-- src:901 | (b) both the fine described in paragraph (a) and imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref Act s 41(1) (src:897-901)
GIVEN `the employer failed to comply with subsection 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer failed to comply with subsection 23(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) — the employer is guilty of an offence` `the employer failed to comply with subsection 21(1)` `the employer failed to comply with subsection 23(3)` MEANS
        `the employer failed to comply with subsection 21(1)`
    OR  `the employer failed to comply with subsection 23(3)`

-- The fine is "in addition to any penalty otherwise provided" and is a ceiling: not exceeding $5,000, with imprisonment of not more
-- than six months in addition if the court so decides.
@ref Act s 41(1) (src:897-901)
GIVEN `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(1) — the most the court may fine the employer` `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(1)` MEANS
    IF `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(1)`
    THEN JUST 5000
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 41(1) (src:897-901)
GIVEN `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(1) — the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that may be imposed with the fine` `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(1)` MEANS
    IF `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(1)`
    THEN JUST 6
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:902 | Idem
-- src:903 | (2) Every person who fails to comply with or contravenes section 24 or 25 is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Act s 41(2) (src:902-903)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 24` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(2) — the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 24` `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 25` MEANS
        `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 24`
    OR  `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 25`

-- Subsection (2) names no fine and no term: "punishable on summary conviction" only. What a summary conviction carries when the
-- offence section is silent is in a general Act that is not deposited (fork F27), so the rule answers NOTHING, never a figure.
@ref Act s 41(2) (src:902-903)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(2) — the most the court may fine the person` `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(2)` MEANS
    NOTHING

-- src:904 | Idem
-- src:905 | (3) Every person who fails to comply with or contravenes section 30 or a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than twenty-five dollars a day for each day of default, but not exceeding in all one thousand dollars.
@ref Act s 41(3) (src:904-905)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with or contravened a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) — the person is guilty of an offence` `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 30` `the person failed to comply with or contravened a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c)` MEANS
        `the person failed to comply with or contravened section 30`
    OR  `the person failed to comply with or contravened a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c)`

-- "a fine of not less than twenty-five dollars a day for each day of default, but not exceeding in all one thousand dollars". Where 25
-- dollars a day for the days of default would pass 1,000, the two limits cannot both hold; the cap is taken to govern both (fork F26).
@ref Act s 41(3) (src:904-905)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(3) — the least the court may fine the person` `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(3)` `the number of days of default` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(3)`
    THEN JUST (min 1000 (25 TIMES `the number of days of default`))
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 41(3) (src:904-905)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(3) — the most the court may fine the person` `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(3)` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(3)`
    THEN JUST 1000
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 41(4) -- false statements, destroying records and evasion`

-- src:906 | Idem
-- src:907 | (4) Every person who
-- src:908 | (a) makes, or participates in, assents to or acquiesces in the making of, false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or a regulation,
-- src:909 | (b) to evade payment of a contribution imposed by this Act, destroys, alters, mutilates, secretes or otherwise disposes of the records or books of account of an employer,
-- src:910 | (c) makes, or assents to or acquiesces in the making of, false or deceptive entries, or omits, or assents to or acquiesces in the omission, to enter a material particular, in records or books of account of an employer,
-- src:911 | (d) wilfully, in any manner, evades or attempts to evade, compliance with this Act or payment of contributions imposed by this Act, or
-- src:912 | (e) conspires with any person to commit an offence described in any of paragraphs (a) to (d),
@ref Act s 41(4)(a) to (e) (src:906-912)
GIVEN `the person made, or participated in, assented to or acquiesced in the making of, false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or a regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, to evade payment of a contribution imposed by this Act, destroyed, altered, mutilated, secreted or otherwise disposed of the records or books of account of an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made, or assented to or acquiesced in the making of, false or deceptive entries, or omitted, or assented to or acquiesced in the omission, to enter a material particular, in records or books of account of an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wilfully, in any manner, evaded or attempted to evade compliance with this Act or payment of contributions imposed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person conspired with any person to commit an offence described in paragraphs 41(4)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(4) — the person is guilty of an offence` `the person made, or participated in, assented to or acquiesced in the making of, false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or a regulation` `the person, to evade payment of a contribution imposed by this Act, destroyed, altered, mutilated, secreted or otherwise disposed of the records or books of account of an employer` `the person made, or assented to or acquiesced in the making of, false or deceptive entries, or omitted, or assented to or acquiesced in the omission, to enter a material particular, in records or books of account of an employer` `the person wilfully, in any manner, evaded or attempted to evade compliance with this Act or payment of contributions imposed by this Act` `the person conspired with any person to commit an offence described in paragraphs 41(4)(a) to (d)` MEANS
        `the person made, or participated in, assented to or acquiesced in the making of, false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or a regulation`
    OR  `the person, to evade payment of a contribution imposed by this Act, destroyed, altered, mutilated, secreted or otherwise disposed of the records or books of account of an employer`
    OR  `the person made, or assented to or acquiesced in the making of, false or deceptive entries, or omitted, or assented to or acquiesced in the omission, to enter a material particular, in records or books of account of an employer`
    OR  `the person wilfully, in any manner, evaded or attempted to evade compliance with this Act or payment of contributions imposed by this Act`
    OR  `the person conspired with any person to commit an offence described in paragraphs 41(4)(a) to (d)`

-- (f): "a fine of not less than twenty-five dollars and not more than five thousand dollars plus, in an appropriate case, an amount not
-- exceeding double the amount of the contribution that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded".
-- Whether the case is "appropriate" is the court's judgment: a conditional input, never guessed.
-- src:913 | is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to
-- src:914 | (f) a fine of not less than twenty-five dollars and not more than five thousand dollars plus, in an appropriate case, an amount not exceeding double the amount of the contribution that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded, or
-- src:915 | (g) both the fine described in paragraph (f) and imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref Act s 41(4)(f) (src:913-915)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(4)(f) — the least the court may fine the person` `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)`
    THEN JUST 25
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 41(4)(f) (src:913-915)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it an appropriate case for an amount in addition to the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the contribution that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(4)(f) — the most the court may fine the person` `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)` `the court considers it an appropriate case for an amount in addition to the fine` `the amount of the contribution that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)`
    THEN JUST (5000 PLUS (IF `the court considers it an appropriate case for an amount in addition to the fine` THEN 2 TIMES `the amount of the contribution that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded` ELSE 0))
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 41(4)(g) (src:913-915)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(4)(g) — the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that may be imposed with the fine` `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 41(4)`
    THEN JUST 6
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 41(5) and (6) -- saving, and who may lay the information`

-- (5): a person convicted of failing to comply with subsection 21(1) or a regulation under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c) is not liable to the
-- penalty under section 21 or under a regulation made under section 40 for the same failure, unless assessed for that penalty or it
-- was demanded before the information or complaint was laid.
-- src:916 | Saving provision
-- src:917 | (5) Where a person has been convicted under this section of failing to comply with subsection 21(1) or a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c), he is not liable to pay any penalty imposed under section 21 or under any regulation made under section 40 for the same failure unless he was assessed for that penalty or that penalty was demanded from him before the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made.
@ref Act s 41(5) (src:916-917)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted under section 41 of failing to comply with subsection 21(1) or a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person was assessed for the penalty or the penalty was demanded from the person, if either happened` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(5) — the person is not liable to pay the penalty for the same failure` `the person has been convicted under section 41 of failing to comply with subsection 21(1) or a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c)` `the day the person was assessed for the penalty or the penalty was demanded from the person, if either happened` `the day the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made` MEANS
        `the person has been convicted under section 41 of failing to comply with subsection 21(1) or a regulation made under paragraph 40(1)(b) or (c)`
    AND (CONSIDER `the day the person was assessed for the penalty or the penalty was demanded from the person, if either happened`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST assessedOrDemanded THEN assessedOrDemanded AT LEAST `the day the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made`)

-- src:918 | Information or complaint
-- src:919 | (6) An information or complaint under this section may be laid or made by any officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or any person thereunto authorized by the Minister and, where an information or complaint purports to have been laid or made under this section, it shall be deemed to have been laid or made by a person thereunto authorized by the Minister and shall not be called in question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Minister or a person acting for him or Her Majesty.
@ref Act s 41(6) (src:918-919)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(6) — the person may lay or make an information or complaint under section 41` `the person is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` `the person is a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` `the person is authorized by the Minister` MEANS
        `the person is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    OR  `the person is a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police`
    OR  `the person is authorized by the Minister`

-- "it shall be deemed to have been laid or made by a person thereunto authorized by the Minister and shall not be called in question for
-- lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Minister or a person acting for him or Her Majesty."
-- The subsection speaks only of an information or complaint that purports to have been laid under section 41; for any other the
-- text does not decide who may call its authority in question, so the answer is NOTHING.
@ref Act s 41(6) (src:918-919)
GIVEN `the information or complaint purports to have been laid or made under section 41` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person calling it in question is the Minister or a person acting for the Minister or Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(6) — the person may call in question the informant's or complainant's lack of authority` `the information or complaint purports to have been laid or made under section 41` `the person calling it in question is the Minister or a person acting for the Minister or Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the information or complaint purports to have been laid or made under section 41`
    THEN JUST `the person calling it in question is the Minister or a person acting for the Minister or Her Majesty`
    ELSE NOTHING
